{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Summary\n\nImporting `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/outbound_differ.py` fails at line ~38 with `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'rebar_reconciler.outbound_comments'`, surfacing as a pytest COLLECTION ERROR on `tests/scripts/reducer/test_managed_refs.py` during a full-suite run. Discovered while landing the open-bugs batch (reducer-cache / linter / perf / reconcile-test fixes).\n\n## Reproduction Steps\n\n1. Fresh venv on current main: `python3 -m venv .venv && .venv/bin/pip install -e '.[dev]'`.\n2. `.venv/bin/pytest tests/scripts/reducer/test_managed_refs.py -q` (or a full-suite run).\n\n## Expected vs Actual\n\n- **Expected:** the module imports and the test collects/runs (or skips) cleanly.\n- **Actual:** `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'rebar_reconciler.outbound_comments'` raised from `outbound_differ.py`, erroring the whole test module at collection.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] `import rebar_reconciler.outbound_differ` succeeds (no ModuleNotFoundError) on a fresh install from main.\n- [x] The symbols the importer needs (e.g. `_normalize_comment_body`) resolve to their real definition location; the import points at the correct module.\n- [x] `tests/scripts/reducer/test_managed_refs.py` collects and runs (passes/skips) rather than erroring at import.\n- [x] A regression test guards the import/collection so the breakage cannot silently recur.\n- [x] No regression in `tests/scripts/reducer/`."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786289812327728001,"uuid":"a7db3580-fc4d-46c6-bec5-cddf45bb23dc"}